  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "A day from morning to night",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Read this sequence out loud once, then close the book and describe your own day. It's fine if it's only five sentences — what matters is that they're yours, not Ani's."
        },
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Georgian",
            "Say it",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "შვიდ საათზე ვდგები",
              "shvid saatze vdgebi",
              "I get up at seven"
            ],
            [
              "ვსაუზმობ",
              "vsauzmob",
              "I have breakfast"
            ],
            [
              "უნივერსიტეტში მივდივარ",
              "universit'et'shi mivdivar",
              "I go to the university"
            ],
            [
              "ქართულს ვსწავლობ",
              "kartuls vsts'avlob",
              "I study Georgian"
            ],
            [
              "შუადღეს ვსადილობ",
              "shuadghes vsadilob",
              "At midday I have lunch"
            ],
            [
              "საღამოს სახლში ვბრუნდები",
              "saghamos sakhlshi vbrundebi",
              "In the evening I go back home"
            ],
            [
              "ვვახშმობ",
              "vvakhshmob",
              "I have dinner"
            ],
            [
              "წიგნს ვკითხულობ",
              "ts'igns vk'itkhulob",
              "I read a book"
            ],
            [
              "თერთმეტ საათზე ვიძინებ",
              "tertmet' saatze vidzineb",
              "At eleven I go to sleep"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Five questions to get other people talking",
          "items": [
            "**რას აკეთებ?** — What are you doing?",
            "**სად მუშაობ?** — Where do you work?",
            "**რას სწავლობ?** — What do you study?",
            "**როდის დგები?** — What time do you get up?",
            "**საღამოს რას აკეთებ?** — What do you do in the evening?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Notice that each of the three meals has its own verb: **ვსაუზმობ** (have breakfast), **ვსადილობ** (have lunch), **ვვახშმობ** (have dinner) — from the nouns საუზმე, სადილი, ვახშამი. Georgian often makes verbs straight from nouns, like English \"to breakfast\", and you'll see this pattern a lot."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
